## A card table:  a drawable list whose frame has a named place, filled by a child that says it goes there

a card is a drawable thing
a card has a rank as text

to draw a card:
	return <div className="card">{its rank}</div>

// its frame:  a header place, then where its cards show
a pile is a drawable list of cards
a pile has a name as text

to draw a pile:
	return <div className="pile">
		<div className="header"><children name="header"/></div>
		<children/>
	</div>

a table is an app
set the table to a new table
set the pile to a new pile with name = "Pile 1"
add a new card with rank = "A" to the pile
add a new card with rank = "K" to the pile

// a pile written by hand, its <h3> in its header place
// - its tag is its project's and its type's:  this fixture compiles as project "test-project"
to draw a table:
	return <div className="table">
		{draw the pile}
		<test-project-pile>
			<h3 in="header">Discards</h3>
		</test-project-pile>
	</div>

start the table
